📊 CUSTOMER ANALYSIS FRAMEWORK - DATA EXTRACTION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

When get_customer_history(email) is called, extract and analyze:

1. BOOKING FREQUENCY ANALYSIS
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Total Bookings: Count of all historical bookings

   Frequency Score:
   - 0 bookings → NEW (tier 1)
   - 1 booking → EXPLORING (tier 1)
   - 2-5 bookings → RECURRING (tier 2)
   - 6-15 bookings → LOYAL (tier 3)
   - 15+ bookings → POWER (tier 3)

   Recency Score:
   - Last booking < 1 week → ACTIVE
   - Last booking < 1 month → ENGAGED
   - Last booking < 3 months → MODERATE
   - Last booking > 3 months → DORMANT
   - No recent booking → INACTIVE


2. SERVICE PREFERENCE ANALYSIS
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Most Booked Service: Count service types

   Service Distribution:
   - "Consulta": 60% of bookings → STRONG preference
   - "Soporte Técnico": 30% of bookings → MODERATE preference
   - "Demostración": 10% of bookings → OCCASIONAL interest

   Confidence Level:
   - If 1 service = 70%+ of bookings → HIGH confidence in recommendation
   - If 2 services = 80%+ → MEDIUM confidence (show top 2)
   - If 3+ services = varied → LOW confidence (show all equally)


3. TIME PREFERENCE ANALYSIS
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Preferred Day of Week:
   - Count bookings by day
   - "Miércoles": 40% of bookings → Strong preference
   - "Viernes": 35% of bookings → Secondary preference

   Preferred Time of Day:
   - Morning (8-12): 50% of bookings → "Morning person"
   - Afternoon (12-17): 30% of bookings → "Afternoon person"
   - Evening (17-21): 20% of bookings → "Evening person"

   Time Pattern:
   - Always same time → Extremely consistent (high confidence)
   - Varies ±1 hour → Flexible within range
   - Varies ±4+ hours → No clear pattern


4. RELIABILITY ANALYSIS
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Cancellation Rate:
   - (Total cancellations / Total bookings) × 100
   - 0% → RELIABLE
   - 1-20% → MOSTLY RELIABLE
   - 21-50% → INCONSISTENT
   - 50%+ → AT RISK

   No-Show Count:
   - 0 no-shows → Perfect attendance
   - 1 no-show → Isolated incident (forgivable)
   - 2+ no-shows → Pattern of unreliability

   Completion Rate:
   - Percentage of bookings that were completed (not cancelled/no-show)
   - <70% → High risk
   - 70-85% → Moderate risk
   - 85-95% → Good reliability
   - 95%+ → Excellent reliability


5. SPENDING ANALYSIS (if available)
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Total Revenue:
   - Sum of all booking values
   - High spender? → VIP treatment
   - Low spender? → Entry-level customer

   Average Booking Value:
   - Could indicate preference for premium services


6. INACTIVITY DETECTION
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Last Booking Date: When was most recent booking?

   Dormancy Status:
   - < 1 week → ACTIVE
   - 1-4 weeks → ENGAGED
   - 1-3 months → MODERATE
   - 3-6 months → DORMANT
   - 6+ months → INACTIVE (re-engagement needed)

   Re-engagement Trigger:
   IF last_booking > 6 months:
     → Flag for re-engagement strategy
     → Offer special incentive to return
     → Check if pain points exist


